# 
# http://purl.org/spar/cito/AffilationSelfCitation
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AffilationSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AffilationSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/spar/cito/SelfCitation> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AffilationSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A citation in which at least one author from each of the citing and the cited entities is affiliated with the same academic institution.\n\nIn particular, like the ancestor class cito:Citation, cito:AffiliationSelfCitation and its accompanying object properties cito:hasCitingEntity, cito:hasCitedEntity and cito:hasCitationCharacterization can be employed to reify direct citation statements made using the CiTO citation object property cito:cites or one of its sub-properties, accompanied by an additional statement using cito:sharesAuthorInstitutionWith for linking the citing paper and the cited paper. \n\nFor example, the following cito:AffiliationSelfCitation resource\n\n     :thisCitation a cito:AffiliationSelfCitation ; \n          cito:hasCitingEntity :paperA ;\n          cito:hasCitationCharacterization cito:extends ;\n          cito:hasCitedEntity :paperB .\n\ncan be alternatively described as follows\n\n     :paperA cito:extends :paperB .\n     :paperA cito:sharesAuthorInstitutionWith :paperB ."@en .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AffilationSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "affilation self citation"@en .
# 
# http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/spar/cito/SelfCitation> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid430 .
_:genid430 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onDataRange> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger> .
_:genid430 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid430 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.org/spar/cito/hasCoAuthorshipCitationLevel> .
_:genid430 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "Derived from the article 'A Small World of Citations? The Influence of Collaboration Networks on Citation Practices' by Matthew L. Wallace, Vincent Larivière and Yves Gingras, published in PLOS One (https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0033339)."@en .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A citation in which at least one author of the citing entity has direct or indirect co-authorship links with one of the authors of the cited entity."@en .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorNetworkSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "author network self citation"@en .
# 
# http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorSelfCitation
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/spar/cito/SelfCitation> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A citation in which the citing and the cited entities have at least one author in common.\n\nIn particular, like the ancestor class cito:Citation, cito:AuthorSelfCitation and its accompanying object properties cito:hasCitingEntity, cito:hasCitedEntity and cito:hasCitationCharacterization can be employed to reify direct citation statements made using the CiTO citation object property cito:cites or one of its sub-properties, accompanied by an additional statement using cito:sharesAuthorWith for linking the citing paper and the cited paper. \n\nFor example, the following cito:AuthorSelfCitation resource\n\n     :thisCitation a cito:AuthorSelfCitation ; \n          cito:hasCitingEntity :paperA ;\n          cito:hasCitationCharacterization cito:extends ;\n          cito:hasCitedEntity :paperB .\n\ncan be alternatively described as follows\n\n     :paperA cito:extends :paperB .\n     :paperA cito:sharesAuthorWith :paperB ."@en .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/AuthorSelfCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "author self citation"@en .
# 
# http://purl.org/spar/cito/Citation
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/Citation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/spar/cito/Citation> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> _:genid431 .
_:genid431 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:genid431 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> _:genid438 .
_:genid438 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid436 .
_:genid436 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid434 .
_:genid434 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid432 .
